---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import PageHero from '../../components/PageHero.astro';
import { breadcrumbSchema, pageSchema } from '../../lib/schema';

const crumbs = [{ label: 'About Evergreen Counseling Collective' }];
---

<Layout
 title="About Evergreen Counseling Collective | Fort Collins, Colorado"
 description="Learn about Evergreen Counseling Collective, a private counseling practice for adults in Fort Collins, Colorado."
 schema={pageSchema([breadcrumbSchema(crumbs, Astro.url.pathname)])}
>
 <PageHero
 eyebrow="About the practice"
 title="A private counseling practice with room for individual attention."
 intro="Evergreen Counseling Collective is Maya Bennett’s counseling practice in Fort Collins, Colorado, offering individual therapy for adults."
 crumbs={crumbs}
 />

 <section class="section">
 <div class="container grid grid--2">
 <div>
 <p class="eyebrow">What you can expect</p>
 <h2>Counseling centered on the reason you came in.</h2>
 </div>

 <div>
 <p>
 Therapy begins with understanding what has been happening in your
 life and what you would like to be different. Some concerns are
 specific and easy to name. Others become clearer over time.
 </p>

 <p>
 You and Maya can decide together what deserves attention, what pace
 feels manageable, and what kind of support may be useful.
 </p>
 </div>
 </div>
 </section>

 <section class="section section--tint">
 <div class="container grid grid--3">
 <article class="card">
 <h3>Individual counseling</h3>
 <p>
 Evergreen Counseling Collective provides one-to-one counseling for adults. The
 work stays focused on your experiences, concerns, and goals.
 </p>
 </article>

 <article class="card">
 <h3>A collaborative process</h3>
 <p>
 Therapy is something you participate in rather than something done
 to you. Questions, preferences, uncertainty, and feedback are
 welcome.
 </p>
 </article>

 <article class="card">
 <h3>Respect for what matters to you</h3>
 <p>
 Your relationships, values, culture, beliefs, and life circumstances
 can all be relevant to counseling without requiring you to fit a
 particular mold.
 </p>
 </article>
 </div>
 </section>

 <section class="section">
 <div class="container grid grid--2">
 <div>
 <p class="eyebrow">Choosing where to begin</p>
 <h2>You do not need to know exactly what kind of therapy you need.</h2>
 </div>

 <div>
 <p>
 The Services page describes common concerns people may bring to
 counseling, including trauma, anxiety, grief, relationship concerns,
 life transitions, low mood, chronic health challenges, and personal
 growth.
 </p>

 <p>
 Maya’s clinician profile explains more about her therapeutic style and
 the approaches she may draw from during counseling. Both pages are
 starting points rather than requirements for knowing exactly what you
 need before reaching out.
 </p>

 <div class="about-links">
 <a class="link-arrow" href="/services/">
 Explore therapy services
 </a>
 </div>
 </div>
 </div>
 </section>

 <section class="section section--tint">
 <div class="container grid grid--2">
 <div>
 <p class="eyebrow">Evergreen Counseling Collective in Fort Collins</p>
 <h2>Learn more about the counselor behind the practice.</h2>
 </div>

 <div>
 <p>
 Evergreen Counseling Collective is Maya Bennett’s private counseling practice.
 Her clinical style, professional presentation, and therapeutic background
 are described on her profile.
 </p>

 <a class="link-arrow" href="/about/maya-bennett/">
 Meet Maya Bennett, LPC
 </a>
 </div>
 </div>
 </section>
</Layout>

<style>
 .about-links{
 display:grid;
 gap:.5rem;
 margin-top:1.25rem
 }
</style>
